Four-character Sino-Korean idioms (사자성어) with Hangul readings and
meanings, from https://github.com/LiF-Lee/idioms (MIT, (c) 2021 EliF).
2,318 entries, idioms.json verbatim.

Vocabularily necessary and permissively licensed: hanja/ covers one syllable
at a time, krdict/ covers words the National Institute dictionary happens to
carry, and neither covers the common four-character idioms.

Input for tools/idioms2data.py; see libhunmin/data/idioms/LICENSE.md for the
extraction contract and the coverage limit. sha256 of idioms.json is in
SHA256SUMS and is also recorded in the converted output's meta.
